Thought:[32;1m[1;3mFinal Answer:
Let $x_i$ denote the production quantity of product $i$ ($i = $ P1, P2, ..., P111$). All $x_i \geq 0$ and continuous.

Maximize total monthly profit:
$$
\max \sum_{i=1}^{111} p_i x_i
$$
where $p_i$ is the Unit_Profit of product $i$ from unit_product_profits.csv.

Subject to device processing time constraints (for each device $d$ = A, B, ..., J):
$$
\sum_{i=1}^{111} a_{d,i} x_i \leq c_d \qquad \forall d \in \{\text{A},\text{B},\text{C},\text{D},\text{E},\text{F},\text{G},\text{H},\text{I},\text{J}\}
$$
where $a_{d,i}$ is the processing time required by product $i$ on device $d$ (from device_time.csv), and $c_d$ is the Monthly_Capacity of device $d$ (from monthly_device_capacity.csv).

Nonnegativity:
$$
x_i \geq 0 \qquad \forall i = 1,\ldots,111
$$

---

