Thought:[32;1m[1;3mFinal Answer:

Let $x_p \geq 0$ be the production quantity of product $p$ ($p \in \{\text{P1}, \text{P2}, \ldots, \text{P111}\}$), continuous and nonnegative.

Maximize total monthly profit:
$$
\max \sum_{p} \text{Unit\_Profit}_p \cdot x_p
$$

where $\text{Unit\_Profit}_p$ is given below for each product.

Subject to device capacity constraints (for each device $d \in \{\text{A},\ldots,\text{J}\}$):
$$
\sum_{p} \text{Time}_{d,p} \cdot x_p \leq \text{Monthly\_Capacity}_d \qquad \forall d
$$

where $\text{Time}_{d,p}$ is the processing time required by product $p$ on device $d$, and $\text{Monthly\_Capacity}_d$ is the monthly capacity of device $d$.

And
$$
x_p \geq 0 \qquad \forall p
$$

